		{
			"id": "111223196316385813",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://hackers.town/@randomgeek/111223196265211968",
			"author": {
				"name": "Random Geek",
				"url": "https://hackers.town/@randomgeek",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/773/610/553/483/original/b4b0269e9d69fb49.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-12T17:21:30.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The interesting bit for me is the reply functionality. For a while I used <a href=\"https://brid.gy\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">brid.gy</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a> as part of an IndieWeb-style commenting system, but stopped when I thought about the consent aspect. Folks assume a Fediverse context, not someone's blog.</p><p>How does WP handle that, I wonder without wondering enough to actually try it.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111223222760903676",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mstdn.social/@josephholsten/111223222482661409",
			"author": {
				"name": ": j@fabrica:~/src;  :t_blink:",
				"url": "https://mstdn.social/@josephholsten",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-12T17:28:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> But if you’re following via activitypub, you can experience the Joy &amp; Wonder of all the comments from everyone everywhere!<br>Btw, these are nothing like pingbacks. They’re totally different and will never be used exclusively for spam.<br>Yep, it’s going to be great…</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111223227523031525",
