			"date": "2023-10-12T17:29:27.625Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://hackers.town/@randomgeek\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>randomgeek</span></a></span> yes, that makes a lot of sense. But would it feel as if my blog is a separate identity from me when those conversations happen? Is it better to spread my identity across two accounts like that?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111223253924907141",
			"parentId": 0,
